      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should probably start with explaining that Gerrit\u0027s existing built-in search capabilities only extend to Change metadata. Then continue with what you have here and explain there\u0027s no way to search for data not in a Change and in the underlying git repo itself.\n\nOr, likely better, put most of that in the background and keep this even shorter with just the second sentence:\n```\nUsers need to search across the repositories and branches they\nare allowed to read, with results respecting Gerrit\u0027s existing project and\nbranch/ref access rules, including private or restricted refs, and the\nsolution must work for large installations with many repositories and\nbranches.\n```",
